    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, the Austin Waves are leaning heavily on **Kyle Tucker** (75.13) and **Andy Pages** (72.13) to anchor the outfield. Both benefit immensely from a high-efficiency matchup against Pfaadt, whose profile offers a rare dual-threat advantage: the park factors remain favorable, and the combination of the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery and favorable platoon splits creates an ideal environment for both hitters to hunt stolen bases. **Jacob Wilson** (68.73) and **Jackson Merrill** (64.64) also project as elite starts; **Jacob Wilson** thrives in the #2 hole with a solid SP matchup, while **Jackson Merrill** gains significant value from a +13% dynamic platoon boost that outweighs a slight park-related downgrade.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Sam Antonacci** (43.60), who narrowly missed the cut. While his lead-off spot against Williams provided a high-upside floor, the sheer defensive and matchup-driven efficiency of **Jorge Polanco** and **Luis Robert Jr.** against the porous Chandler (xERA 4.97) forced him to the pine. We are exercising caution with **Heliot Ramos** (47.64), whose score remains muted due to a daunting assignment against Sale. Despite the low projected floor, we are rolling him out to maintain category coverage, though his status warrants monitoring if the early innings suggest Sale is in mid-season form.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in our top-tier matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** faces an elite challenge in deGrom, and despite his strong lineup placement, the -19% SP skill penalty necessitates a tempered outlook for his counting stats. Furthermore, we continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who is currently out of the starting rotation. With SB being the primary scarcity focus for the Austin Waves, our reliance on the speed profiles of **Andy Pages** and **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014bolstered by the projected slow deliveries of their opposing pitchers\u2014is the engine driving today's tactical deployment.",
